WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.427
Apple Silicon systems can run local chat interfaces, web UIs, local inference APIs, coding tools, document workflows, and private assistants.

00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:16.314
Once a local model is served through an endpoint, it can become part of a broader application workflow.

00:00:16.314 --> 00:00:19.857
That is useful, but it also changes the risk profile.

00:00:19.857 --> 00:00:23.468
The model is no longer only an interactive experiment.

00:00:23.468 --> 00:00:25.941
It is a service other tools may call.

00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:33.563
Localhost binding is a safer default for private inference services because it limits access to the local machine.

00:00:33.563 --> 00:00:39.447
LAN access can be useful for a homelab or team environment, but it should be deliberate.

00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:47.470
Reverse proxies, authentication, TLS, and access policy may be needed at a high level if other users or devices connect.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:52.418
Avoid accidental exposure of a local model endpoint to untrusted networks.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:56.630
Applications that call local models should be scoped carefully.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:05.522
A coding tool, document assistant, or private chat interface may send sensitive prompts, files, or context to the inference endpoint.

00:01:05.522 --> 00:01:17.891
If several applications share one local service, operators should understand which data flows through it, whether logs are retained, and whether different workflows should be separated.

00:01:17.891 --> 00:01:21.568
Serving local models is not just a convenience feature.

00:01:21.568 --> 00:01:28.789
It requires decisions about access control, logging, retention, uptime, update timing, and failure behavior.

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:32.533
Treat prompts and outputs as potentially sensitive data.

00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:41.359
Local inference can improve privacy, but only when service exposure and surrounding application behavior are managed with intention.
